 ops/changelog.md | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/ops/changelog.md b/ops/changelog.md
index 84cd968ce2..465e011a55 100644
--- a/ops/changelog.md
+++ b/ops/changelog.md
@@ -10482,3 +10482,4 @@ Did NOT modify research-roadmap.yaml or scripts/research_conductor.py. Did NOT p
 - 2026-06-30: PHASE D1 (VERIFIER MOAT; PRIMARY HEADLINE) -- TRAIN the REAL arXiv:2605.18871 LoRA-EBM holistic-quality scorer FOR REAL this time (the .461 D1 bootstrap-and-bailed = skeleton, never trained). Qwen3.5-1.7B base + LoRA + scalar energy head, contrastive on FoVer + gold-labeled candidate pairs; EVAL min-energy select vs the GENUINE tuned-SC (B1). The decisive open question: does a TRAINED oracle-distinct verifier capture the MuSR headroom? TRAIN-FIRST-NOT-SKELETON-FIRST; the gate REQUIRES train_loss non-null + duration>60s. (⚠️ Blocked) — honest_verdict=blocked_trainable_qwen_base; results/experiment_5017_lora_ebm_scorer_musr_v2.json
 - 2026-06-30: PHASE D2 (VERIFIER MOAT; the published WIN-CONDITION existence proof) -- REPLICATE uPRM (arXiv:2605.10158) UNBLOCKED: the .461 D2 blocked only on the empty logprob cache (the scorer + first-error formula are fully implemented). Consume the B2 shared logprob cache, run the uPRM next-token-prob first-error process score as an oracle-distinct SELECTOR over K candidates, gate beats-GENUINE-tuned-SC with McNemar CI95-excl-0 on MuSR. LC-ERD (arXiv:2605.24005) consistency-based fallback if logprobs are incomplete. (⚠️ Blocked) — honest_verdict=blocked_b2_logprob_cache; results/experiment_5018_uprm_replication_v2.json
 - 2026-06-30: PHASE D6 (VERIFIER MOAT; the EFFICIENCY axis -- north-star §5 Pareto win) -- build the uncertainty-routed cheap-verifier -> strong-judge CASCADE (arXiv:2510.20369): the cheap oracle-distinct verifier selects when confident and routes ONLY uncertain questions to a strong LLM-judge. The WIN = accuracy parity (within CI) with the judge-only baseline at MATERIALLY FEWER judge calls. Charge the judge-call budget explicitly so the judge cannot become the moat (the E1 pitfall). (⚠️ Blocked) — honest_verdict=blocked_judge_server; results/experiment_5020_uncertainty_routed_cascade.json
+- 2026-06-30: PHASE D4 (VERIFIER MOAT; CROSS-CORPUS GENERALIZATION) -- evaluate the BEST D1/D2/D3 oracle-distinct verifier on a SECOND headroom-present oracle-distinct corpus (GPQA / MMLU-Pro-hard / MATH-500-hard, whichever is cached + headroom_present vs the GENUINE tuned-SC). The gate requires MuSR + >=1 second corpus: a single-corpus win could be corpus-specific. Honest MuSR-scoped record if no 2nd corpus is headroom-present. (⚠️ Blocked) — honest_verdict=blocked_no_best_verifier; results/experiment_5021_moat_second_corpus_v2.json
